Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 08:55:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 2311: every wording of an introduction is one; the server
 never sends it as a question
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Box 54162, 2 of 5: „სთხოვე ლევანს, დამაკავშიროს თამთასთან" and „მაიას თხოვე
ბახვასთან დაკავშირება" were not read as introductions (the detector knew
only „დამაკავშირე", and a verb form inside a longer word could match), so
the run's ask was not turned to request_introduction and the server's
unsent-instruction fallback sent the owner's line as a plain question.
- the detector reads დამაკავშიროს, დაგვაკავშიროს, შემაერთე, შემაერთოს,
  შეგვაერთოს and „…თან დაკავშირება/გაცნობა"; each verb form must end the
  word, so „შემაერთებს თუ არა" stays a question (Case 1's rule);
- the fallback never sends an introduction as its own plain question; it
  says the existing not-sent line instead.
No new text.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
